      "facts": [
        "Luke 21 combines temple destruction, conflict, witness, Jerusalem's siege, cosmic imagery, Son of Man expectation, and watchfulness; it cannot securely identify a current nation, conspiracy, date, party, or territorial entitlement.",
        "Dates around 70-100 CE are common, but proposed dates range from before 70 CE into the early second century and depend on Synoptic relations, temple language, Acts, and reception.",
        "Luke places the widow's temple gift immediately after condemning scribes who consume widows' houses and before temple judgment; praise, lament, and institutional exposure remain debated, so the story cannot coerce poor people to surrender necessities."
